---
// /welding-estimate-calculator/ — 焊工估价计算器（免费工具页）
// 与 /invoice-calculator/ 同构,但按焊接行业定价模型定制:
// 分工序工价(MIG/TIG/Stick) + 钢材耗材加价 + 动员费 + 50% 定金(匹配模板 depositPct)
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Welding Estimate Calculator — Free Welding Estimator |';
const description = 'Free welding estimator & estimate calculator. Enter MIG, TIG and stick hours, steel and consumables, mobilization and tax — get subtotal, 50% deposit and';
const canonical = 'https://fieldformtemplates.com/welding-estimate-calculator/';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <section class="section wrap" style="padding-top:40px;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.4px;color:var(--teal);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px;">Free Tool</p>
      <h1>Welding Estimate Calculator</h1>
      <p class="lead">A free welding estimator for small shops and mobile welders — price a job in two minutes with labor by process (MIG, TIG, stick), steel and consumables with markup, mobilization, tax, and the 50% deposit to ask for at signing. No signup, no email, works offline.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:30px;gap:32px;align-items:start;">
      <div class="card" style="padding:28px;">
        <h2 style="font-size:20px;margin-bottom:20px;">Your costs</h2>
        <div style="margin-bottom:24px;">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;">Welding labor — by process</p>
          <div id="labor-list">
            <div class="labor-row" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 90px 100px 32px;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px;align-items:end;">
              <input type="text" class="labor-name calc-input" value="MIG / flux-core" style="font-size:14px;" />
              <input type="number" class="labor-hrs calc-input" min="0" step="0.5" value="4" placeholder="Hrs" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <input type="number" class="labor-rate calc-input" min="0" step="5" value="70" placeholder="$/hr" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <button class="labor-del" style="padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;">×</button>
            </div>
            <div class="labor-row" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 90px 100px 32px;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px;align-items:end;">
              <input type="text" class="labor-name calc-input" value="TIG (stainless / aluminum)" style="font-size:14px;" />
              <input type="number" class="labor-hrs calc-input" min="0" step="0.5" value="2" placeholder="Hrs" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <input type="number" class="labor-rate calc-input" min="0" step="5" value="95" placeholder="$/hr" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <button class="labor-del" style="padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;">×</button>
            </div>
            <div class="labor-row" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 90px 100px 32px;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px;align-items:end;">
              <input type="text" class="labor-name calc-input" value="Stick (SMAW)" style="font-size:14px;" />
              <input type="number" class="labor-hrs calc-input" min="0" step="0.5" value="6" placeholder="Hrs" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <input type="number" class="labor-rate calc-input" min="0" step="5" value="60" placeholder="$/hr" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <button class="labor-del" style="padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;">×</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p id="labor-line" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:8px;">12 hrs across 3 processes = $610.00</p>
          <button id="add-labor" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--accent);background:none;border:none;cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:4px 0;">+ Add process line</button>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:24px;">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;">Materials &amp; consumables</p>
          <div id="materials-list">
            <div class="mat-row" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 100px 32px;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px;align-items:end;">
              <input type="text" class="mat-name calc-input" placeholder="Item (e.g. Steel plate 3/8&quot;)" value="Steel stock / plate" style="font-size:14px;" />
              <input type="number" class="mat-cost calc-input" min="0" step="0.01" value="240" placeholder="Cost $" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <button class="mat-del" style="padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;">×</button>
            </div>
            <div class="mat-row" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 100px 32px;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px;align-items:end;">
              <input type="text" class="mat-name calc-input" placeholder="Item (e.g. Rod / wire / gas)" value="Rod, wire &amp; shielding gas" style="font-size:14px;" />
              <input type="number" class="mat-cost calc-input" min="0" step="0.01" value="85" placeholder="Cost $" style="font-size:14px;text-align:right;" />
              <button class="mat-del" style="padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;">×</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <button id="add-mat" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--accent);background:none;border:none;cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:4px 0;">+ Add material line</button>
          <div style="margin-top:14px;">
            <label for="markup" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);display:block;margin-bottom:4px;">Markup on materials (%) — covers pickup time and stock risk</label>
            <input id="markup" type="number" min="0" max="200" step="5" value="20" class="calc-input" style="max-width:140px;" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:24px;">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;">Other costs</p>
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;">
            <div>
              <label for="mob" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);display:block;margin-bottom:4px;">Mobilization / travel ($)</label>
              <input id="mob" type="number" min="0" step="5" value="75" class="calc-input" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="misc" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);display:block;margin-bottom:4px;">Prep &amp; finishing ($)</label>
              <input id="misc" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="105" class="calc-input" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:8px;">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;">Deposit &amp; tax</p>
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;">
            <div>
              <label for="deposit" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);display:block;margin-bottom:4px;">Deposit at signing (%)</label>
              <input id="deposit" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="50" class="calc-input" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="tax" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);display:block;margin-bottom:4px;">Sales tax rate (%)</label>
              <input id="tax" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.1" value="0" class="calc-input" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px;">Tax applies to the full subtotal here — if your state taxes materials but not labor, calculate tax on materials only.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:28px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f7ff,#e8f4fe);border-color:#b8d8f5;position:sticky;top:80px;">
        <h2 style="font-size:20px;margin-bottom:20px;">Welding job estimate</h2>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;">
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:15px;">
            <span style="color:var(--muted);">Welding labor</span>
            <span id="r-labor" style="font-weight:600;">$610.00</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:15px;">
            <span style="color:var(--muted);" id="mat-label">Materials (incl. 20% markup)</span>
            <span id="r-materials" style="font-weight:600;">$390.00</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:15px;">
            <span style="color:var(--muted);">Mobilization &amp; prep</span>
            <span id="r-other" style="font-weight:600;">$180.00</span>
          </div>
          <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px;margin-top:4px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:15px;">
            <span style="color:var(--muted);">Subtotal</span>
            <span id="r-subtotal" style="font-weight:600;">$1,180.00</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:15px;">
            <span style="color:var(--muted);" id="tax-label">Tax (0%)</span>
            <span id="r-tax" style="font-weight:600;">$0.00</span>
          </div>
          <div style="border-top:2px solid var(--accent);padding-top:14px;margin-top:4px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;">
            <span style="font-size:18px;font-weight:700;">Total</span>
            <span id="r-total" style="font-size:28px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);">$1,180.00</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:15px;background:#fff;border:1px dashed var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;">
            <span style="color:var(--muted);" id="deposit-label">Deposit at signing (50%)</span>
            <span id="r-deposit" style="font-weight:700;">$590.00</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:15px;">
            <span style="color:var(--muted);">Balance on completion</span>
            <span id="r-balance" style="font-weight:600;">$590.00</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button id="copy-btn" class="btn btn-primary btn-block" style="margin-top:24px;">Copy breakdown to clipboard</button>
        <p id="copy-msg" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--teal);text-align:center;margin-top:8px;display:none;">Copied! Paste into your estimate or notes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap" style="padding-top:40px;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>How to price a welding job</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:24px;">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Labor by process</h3>
        <p>Not all arcs bill the same. Typical US rates: stick $50-$75/hr, MIG and flux-core $60-$90/hr, TIG on stainless or aluminum $75-$125/hr. Field work adds 20-40% over shop rate. Estimate hours per process, not one blended number — customers accept the price faster when they see the split.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Materials &amp; markup</h3>
        <p>Steel stock, filler rod, wire, and shielding gas are billed at cost plus 20-30% — the markup covers pickup time, cutting waste, and the risk of mis-ordered stock. Keep receipts; list anything over $50 as its own line on the estimate so the customer can see what drives the price.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Deposit &amp; terms</h3>
        <p>Ask 30-50% at signing — the higher end whenever you must buy steel or specialty filler upfront, so you never finance the client's project. Hold the quote for 30 days, set Net 10 on the balance, and add a workmanship guarantee (90 days on welded joints is standard) to close the deal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:40px;">
      <h2 style="font-size:22px;margin-bottom:6px;">Welding rate cheat sheet (2024–2025 US midpoints)</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:16px;">Type these rates straight into the estimator above. Field/on-site rates run 20–40% over shop rates; certified welders (AWS D1.1, ASME IX, API 1104) price at the top of each range.</p>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
        <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;">
          <thead>
            <tr>{['Cost line', 'Shop rate', 'Field / mobile rate', 'Deposition rate'].map((h) => <th style="text-align:left;padding:12px 14px;background:var(--soft);border-bottom:2px solid var(--blue);white-space:nowrap;">{h}</th>)}</tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {[
              ['Stick welding (SMAW)', '$50–$75/hr', '$75–$100/hr', '2–4 lb/hr'],
              ['MIG welding (GMAW)', '$60–$90/hr', '$80–$110/hr', '6–12 lb/hr'],
              ['Flux-core (FCAW)', '$60–$85/hr', '$80–$105/hr', '5–9 lb/hr'],
              ['TIG — stainless / aluminum (GTAW)', '$75–$125/hr', '$100–$150/hr', '1–3 lb/hr'],
              ['Cutting & bevel prep', '$45–$60/hr', '$55–$75/hr', '—'],
              ['Grinding & finishing', '$45–$60/hr', '$55–$75/hr', '—'],
            ].map((row) => (
              <tr>{row.map((cell) => <td style="padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;white-space:nowrap;">{cell}</td>)}</tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin-top:12px;">Materials: steel stock at cost +20–30% markup · shielding gas and consumables roughly $0.50–$2.00 per deposited pound · mobile call-out minimums of $150–$300 before the clock starts.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:40px;">
      <h2 style="font-size:22px;margin-bottom:6px;">Three real welding jobs, priced with this estimator</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:15px;margin-bottom:16px;">Each example uses the default rates from the cheat sheet — copy the numbers into the calculator above and check the total for yourself.</p>
      <div class="grid3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px;">Handrail repair (mobile)</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);">Stick 1.5 hr × $85 field + prep/finish 0.5 hr × $60 + $30 consumables marked up 20% + $75 mobilization.</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700;margin-top:8px;">≈ $270 total · $135 deposit</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px;">Trailer floor repair (flux-core)</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);">Flux-core 3 hr × $90 + cutting/prep 1.5 hr × $65 + $180 steel &amp; $45 consumables at +20% + $100 mobilization.</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700;margin-top:8px;">≈ $740 total · $370 deposit</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px;">Shop fabrication (TIG, stainless)</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);">TIG 6 hr × $110 + fit-up 3 hr × $55 + $400 stainless stock &amp; $90 filler/gas at +20% (shop — no mobilization).</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700;margin-top:8px;">≈ $1,410 total · $705 deposit</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:40px;">
      <h2 style="font-size:22px;margin-bottom:6px;">Pricing per inch or per pound instead of hourly</h2>
      <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink);">Once you know your deposition rates, fabrication work prices out faster by the inch of weld or pound of deposited metal: a ¼″ fillet lays down about 0.75 lb of weld per foot, so 40 ft of fillet needs roughly 30 lb of deposit — 3–5 arc-hours on MIG, 15+ on TIG. Multiply by your labor rate, add filler and gas at $0.50–$2.00 per deposited pound, then check the number against your hourly estimate. The two methods should land within 15% of each other; if they don't, your hours estimate is off. The full method with tables is in our <a href="/guides/how-to-write-a-welding-estimate/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">guide to writing welding estimates</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:32px;padding:20px 24px;background:var(--soft);border-radius:12px;">
      <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;"><strong>Put these numbers on paper.</strong> Grab a free <a href="/templates/welder-estimate-template/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">welder estimate template</a>, the matching <a href="/templates/welding-estimate-template/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">welding estimate template</a>, or a firm-price <a href="/templates/welding-quote-template/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">welding quote template</a> — pre-filled with MIG/TIG/stick line items, downloads as Word, Excel, or PDF. No email required. Running the whole job through the shop instead? The <a href="/templates/fabrication-invoice-template/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">metal fabrication invoice template</a> bills shop hours, steel with markup, and CNC cutting as separate lines. For other trades, the general <a href="/invoice-calculator/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">invoice calculator</a> and the full <a href="/estimate-templates/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">estimate template library</a> are also free.</p>
      <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;margin-top:10px;">New to pricing welding work? The step-by-step <a href="/guides/how-to-write-a-welding-estimate/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">welding estimate guide</a> covers hour-estimating methods, process rate tables, and deposit terms in depth.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap" style="padding-top:20px;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Embed this welding estimator on your site</h2>
      <p>Free to embed — useful for welding schools, fabrication blogs and contractor resource pages. Paste this where you want it to appear.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:20px;padding:20px 24px;background:var(--soft);border-radius:12px;">
      <textarea id="embed-code" readonly rows="4" style="width:100%;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:13px;padding:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:#fff;color:var(--ink);resize:vertical;">&lt;iframe src="https://fieldformtemplates.com/welding-estimate-calculator/?embed=1" width="100%" height="900" style="border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:10px;" title="Free welding estimate calculator — FieldForm Templates" loading="lazy"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:13px;color:#6b7280;"&gt;Welding estimator by &lt;a href="https://fieldformtemplates.com/welding-estimate-calculator/"&gt;FieldForm Templates&lt;/a&gt; — free welding quote and estimate templates.&lt;/p&gt;</textarea>
      <div style="margin-top:12px;display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" onclick="(function(){var t=document.getElementById('embed-code');t.select();document.execCommand('copy');if(navigator.clipboard)navigator.clipboard.writeText(t.value);if(window.showToast)showToast('Embed code copied');})()">Copy embed code</button>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/welding-estimate-calculator/?embed=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Preview widget →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap" style="padding-top:20px;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Welding pricing FAQ</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:20px;">
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">What should I charge per hour for welding?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">Typical US ranges: stick/SMAW $50-$75/hr, MIG and flux-core $60-$90/hr, TIG $75-$125/hr. Mobile/on-site welding runs $80-$120/hr because travel and equipment are built in. Certified welders (AWS D1.1, ASME pipe) price at the top of each range. Your rate must cover machine payments, gas, consumables, insurance, and non-billable shop time — not just take-home pay.</p>
      </details>
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">Should I price by the hour or by the inch of weld?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">Hourly suits repair and one-off work — it's predictable and fair when scope is unclear. Production and fabrication work is usually priced per inch of weld, per joint, or per pound of deposited metal once you know your deposition rates. Start hourly with a not-to-exceed cap, track actual hours per joint, and move to per-joint pricing once you have data.</p>
      </details>
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">How much deposit should a welder ask for?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">30-50% at signing is standard. Use 50% when the job requires buying steel stock, plate, or specialty filler upfront — the deposit should cover your material outlay. For pure repair labor with no materials, 25-30% is enough to hold the calendar slot. Always put the deposit amount and balance terms in writing on the estimate.</p>
      </details>
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">Why does TIG cost more than stick or MIG?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">TIG is slower, more skill-dependent, and needs both hands plus a foot pedal — but it produces the cleanest, strongest welds on stainless and aluminum. A TIG hour produces fewer inches of weld than MIG, so the rate must be higher to earn the same. Charge the premium: customers shopping for aluminum or stainless work expect it.</p>
      </details>
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">How much does it cost to weld a handrail?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">A typical steel handrail repair — re-weld a loose post or cracked joint, on-site — runs $150–$350. Most of it is the mobile call-out minimum plus 1–2 stick hours; new powder-coated rail sections add material cost at 20–30% markup. A full custom indoor staircase rail fabrication is a different job: $65–$125 per linear foot installed depending on region and material.</p>
      </details>
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">How much is a mobile welder's minimum call-out?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">$150–$300 for the first hour or two is the national norm, with $1–$2 per loaded mile beyond a 20–30 mile radius. Roadside and emergency call-outs (trailer, gate, equipment breakdowns) run 50–100% over shop rates — often weekend and after-hours multipliers too. Always quote the minimum before dispatching; it filters non-serious callers and covers your travel.</p>
      </details>
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">How do I calculate welding cost per pound of weld?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">Weigh the deposit: for a ¼″ fillet that's about 0.75 lb per foot of weld. Divide by your process's deposition rate (MIG 6–12 lb/hr, stick 2–4 lb/hr, TIG 1–3 lb/hr) to get arc-hours, multiply by your labor rate, then add filler metal and gas at $0.50–$2.00 per deposited pound. Add fit-up, prep and finishing hours at their own rate. The estimator above does the same math in hourly form — both routes should agree within ~15%.</p>
      </details>
      <details style="margin-bottom:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);">
        <summary style="font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;">What's the difference between a welding estimate, a quote, and a bid?</summary>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted);">An estimate is a good-faith range that can move with actual hours and materials — right for repairs with unknown scope. A quote is a fixed price held for a stated window (30 days is standard because steel moves). A bid is a formal proposal against other bidders on contract or code work. The same line items power all three; change the title and how firm the numbers are. Grab the <a href="/templates/welding-quote-template/" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">welding quote template</a> when you need to commit to a number.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
