      { "@type": "Question", name: "What's the difference between a welding estimate, a quote, and a bid?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "An estimate is a good-faith range that can move with actual hours and materials — right for repairs with unknown scope. A quote is a fixed price held for a stated window, usually 30 days. A bid is a formal proposal against other bidders on contract or code work. The same line items power all three." } },
